# TSan suppressions for Snowglobe. Consumed ONLY by the tsan CTest preset
# (test/CMakeLists sets TSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=<this file> for the proxy
# and replay integration tests when built with -fsanitize=thread).
# Debug/asan run fully unsuppressed.
#
# libstdc++ <regex> compiler internal race (CI run 36447650097, test
# proxy_concurrent; same shape re-observed in proxy_notify_concurrent, CI
# run 38027094329, and in replay_concurrent on BOTH toolchains, CI run
# 38064833528): concurrent first-use construction of httplib's
# thread_local response-line regexes (ClientImpl::read_response_line)
# from our per-request upstream threads races inside
# _Compiler/_Scanner/ctype::narrow on libstdc++.so globals.
# Both stacks are third-party frames (httplib const path + libstdc++ regex
# compile); the only snowglobe frames are cli.send (proxy.cpp:481) and
# thread spawn (proxy.cpp:426) — no snowglobe frame touches shared mutable
# state. Our codebase contains zero std::regex / std::locale use, so these
# frames can only ever come from the dependency, and libstdc++ 13 (Ubuntu
# 24.04 tsan, same test) is clean. Revisit on any toolchain or
# cpp-httplib version bump.
race:std::__detail::_Compiler*
race:std::__detail::_Scanner*
race:std::ctype<char>::narrow*
